A better scheduling question is: **Which activities require another activity to finish, which can overlap without competing for the same equipment or operator, and which materials or conditions must be prepared, chilled, equilibrated, rested, or ready at a precise time?** Applied here, the heat block must be at 95 °C before denaturation; samples must be thawed before denaturation and spun before loading; chilled transfer buffer must be ready one hour into the gel run; the PVDF and transfer pads must be prepared before the transfer sandwich is built; the sandwich must wait until five minutes after the run ends; the membrane must remain in the cold room during the overnight primary incubation; ECL must be mixed 50 minutes into secondary incubation so it is ready after the final wash; and all rocker, transfer-tank, cold-room, imager, and bench activities must respect their single-use limits. No additional inferred activity is required beyond the explicit preparation and timing requirements, so the heat-block preheating step is included as the one necessary inferred step.

